# Dockerized local dev stack for {{DISPLAY}} (BP §21), fronted by the shared Caddy (BP §20).
# Rules encoded here:
#  - ports bind to 127.0.0.1, so nothing is reachable from the LAN;
#  - source is bind-mounted, node_modules NEVER is: each service gets named
#    volumes for its own modules and store, and every other workspace member's
#    node_modules is shadowed, so a container install can't clobber the host's;
#  - heavy trees a container never reads (native ios/android/macOS output) are
#    masked with empty volumes, so watchers can't exhaust macOS's kern.maxfiles;
#  - healthchecks probe 127.0.0.1, not localhost;
#  - file watching is event-based. Create, edit, rename and delete a file once and
#    watch the logs; only if an event never arrives, run `next dev --webpack`
#    with WATCHPACK_POLLING=true here (Turbopack ignores polling settings).
name: {{CODENAME}}
